{
  "dom_id": "step-q99769",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "$\\frac{(\\frac{7}{4})}{7}=$",
  "worked_solution": "We can use either of the following two methods.\n\n**Method 1 - The Long Way**\n\nFirst, remember that a fraction represents a division:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(\\frac{7}{4})}{7}=\\frac{7}{4}÷7\n$$\n\nNow, recall that dividing by $7$ is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal $\\frac{1}{7}.$ We can use this fact to simplify the fraction above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{4}÷7 & = \\\\ \\frac{7}{4}\\times \\frac{1}{7} & = \\\\ \\frac{7\\times 1}{4\\times 7} & = \\\\ \\frac{7}{28}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{28}=\\frac{7÷7}{28÷7}=\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{(\\frac{7}{4})}{7}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\n**Method 2 - The Quick Way**\n\nThe result will have the same numerator as the top fraction, and the denominator is just the product of the two denominators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(\\frac{7}{4})}{7} & = \\\\ \\frac{7}{4\\times 7} & = \\\\ \\frac{7}{28} & = \\\\ \\frac{7÷7}{28÷7} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
